			<div class="content" id="post-content-1321994">
									

<p>Honestly, I'm a bit on the fence about the memory section, even though it may have come about from a suggestion of mine (honestly, especially since it came about from a suggestion&#8230; I'm an excellent person to tap for grammar but my creative ideas frequently fall flat). I think it might work better if it cut straight to the tossing her up in the air so that it feels more like a small fragment of a memory, cherished, but worn thin by overhandling, clinging to it even as he knows that holding on too tight is making it fall faster from his fingertips. :-P But, as I said, I'm wary of following my own suggestions, so grains of salt and all of that.</p>

